on, Travel), and a list of authored discussions (\\\"Threads by WellnessWanderer (2)\\\") with both her threads shown.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Registered qatester_persist, set bio \\\"QA persistence test bio - FT13/FT18 check.\\\" and interests (Testing, QA, Automation), authored a thread with 1 reply, and upvoted thread-7 (92→93). Logged out then back in with the same credentials: profile page still showed the bio and interest tags, the authored thread \\\"QA Persistence Test Thread FT13/FT18\\\" still listed under \\\"Threads by qatester_persist (1)\\\", the reply still present, and thread-7's vote button still showed the persistent voted-state classes (bg-primary/10 text-primary) with count 93.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-18\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"All application state is lost on page reload instead of persisting\", \"actual\": \"Established state as qatester_persist (registered account, edited bio/interests, authored a thread with a reply, upvoted thread-7 raising it from 92 to 93) then performed a full page reload. After reload: nav bar reverted to logged-out state (Login/Register links); navigating to the account's profile URL directly returned \\\"User not found\\\" (account no longer exists); the home Trending list no longer showed the authored thread at all (back to only the original 8 seed threads); thread-7's upvote count reverted to 92 and its vote button returned to the disabled/unvoted state. This shows the app relies entirely on non-persisted in-memory state — no registered accounts, sign-in sessions, profile edits, authored content, or votes survive a page reload.\", \"evidence\": \"Post-reload snapshot of / showed \\\"Login\\\"/\\\"Register\\\" nav links (not signed in); GET /profile/user-1787620155524 rendered heading \\\"User not found\\\"; Trending list contained only the original 8 seed threads (thread-1 through thread-8), with thread-7 at 92 replies-count unchanged and vote button in disabled/unvoted state.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Submitting with all fields blank, and with only Title filled (no category/body), both showed \\\"Please fill in all fields\\\" toast and no discussion was created (page remained on /new-thread with entered data preserved).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Incorrect password accepted for login\", \"actual\": \"Logging in with qatester1@example.com and an incorrect password (\\\"wrongpassword\\\") succeeded, showing \\\"Welcome back!\\\" toast and a fully logged-in session (New Thread link, profile link for qatester1) instead of being rejected.\", \"evidence\": \"POST login with wrong password still returned authenticated session; nav bar showed logged-in state.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Unauthenticated user is not redirected to a usable sign-in screen when attempting to start a discussion\", \"actual\": \"While logged out, navigating to the New Thread page (/new-thread) renders a completely blank page (only the notification region present) instead of showing the discussion form or redirecting to a sign-in screen. Console shows a React warning \\\"You should call navigate() in a React.useEffect(), not when your component is first rendered,\\\" indicating the intended redirect-to-login logic is implemented incorrectly and fails to execute, leaving the user stuck on a blank page with no way to sign in or proceed.\", \"evidence\": \"URL remained /new-thread after load; snapshot showed no heading, form, or login prompt — page body empty aside from notification region. Console warning referencing an invalid navigate() call during render.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Trending initially ordered 156,124,92,89,78,67,56,48,0 (desc by upvotes). Used 4 separate accounts to upvote thread-2 (89→93), which progressively rose in rank and ended up clearly above thread-7 (92 upvotes, unchanged): new order 156,124,93,92,78,67,56,48,0. Confirms both initial sort and dynamic reorder on vote changes.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Displayed reply total does not match actual replies listed on detail view\", \"actual\": \"Thread-1 (\\\"What programming language should I learn in 2024?\\\") displays \\\"23 replies\\\" in its header/summary, but the detail view's Replies section heading reads \\\"Replies (2)\\\" and only 2 reply items (GameMaster42, NewsHound) are actually rendered. The displayed total (23) does not match the number of replies listed (2).\", \"evidence\": \"Thread header: \\\"23 replies\\\"; Replies section: \\\"Replies (2)\\\" with exactly 2 reply items shown.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No stated time window for Trending/Most Active rankings\", \"actual\": \"Both \\\"Trending Discussions\\\" and \\\"Most Active Discussions\\\" views show only the generic subtitle \\\"Join the conversation with our community\\\" with no indication of a time window (e.g., \\\"last 7 days\\\", \\\"this week\\\"). Rankings appear to be computed from all-time upvote/reply totals rather than a recent window, and no UI text states any such window.\", \"evidence\": \"Page text scanned for time-window phrasing (day/week/hour/recent/last 24/this week) — matches found were incidental (thread body content, \\\"Recent\\\" sort button label), not a stated ranking window.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Community Stats \\\"Members\\\" count does not update when new accounts are created\", \"actual\": \"Registered 5 new accounts during this session (qatester2, qatester_vote1, qatester_vote2, qatester_vote3, qatester_vote4) via the UI, but the \\\"Members\\\" count in Community Stats remained fixed at 892 throughout, never incrementing. By contrast, the \\\"Replies\\\" counter (4,823) did correctly reflect the 5 replies added during testing, showing counts are selectively stale.\", \"evidence\": \"Community Stats panel showed Members: 892 both before and after 5 new registrations; Replies count 4,823 correctly matched additions (1 original QA reply + 4 replies added to thread-3).\"}]}"
